## Rules
- Write all code, comments and Markdown in English. Talk to the user in their language
  (from their Claude settings or instructions; otherwise the language they write in).
- After each working step run corecrew's `save "<message>"` (commits code and docs together;
  Claude runs it; its path is printed at session start, or `<plugin>/scripts/save`).
  To publish: `save "<message>" --push`. `undo-step` reverts the last step in both repos,
  including knowledge and standards edits made in that step.
- After changing a feature, update its page in `{{PROJECT_DIR}}/docs/features/` and its `updated` field.
  After adding or changing any page, run corecrew's `wiki-index.sh {{PROJECT_DIR}}` (it rewrites
  `{{PROJECT_DIR}}/docs/INDEX.md`; script: `<plugin>/scripts/wiki-index.sh`). Never write map lines by hand.
- A new architectural decision gets a new file `{{PROJECT_DIR}}/docs/decisions/NNN-<slug>.md`.
- Put specs in `{{PROJECT_DIR}}/docs/specs/` and plans in `{{PROJECT_DIR}}/docs/plans/`, not in the code repo.
- Links between wiki pages are wikilinks: `[[page-name]]`, `[[page-name#Heading]]`.
- The wiki is `{{PROJECT_DIR}}/docs/`, one wiki for every worktree. Edit it by that absolute path
  from any worktree; `save` run in the worktree commits the wiki with the worktree's code.
- Tests (`**/test/**`, `**/tests/**`, `*_test.*`, `*.test.*`): write the failing test first, watch it
  fail, then implement. Tests must not depend on network access or real accounts. Keep test names
  descriptive: what behavior, under which condition.
- Never read `.env` files or `~/.ssh`.
